# The two JSON databases live in S3 (see backend/store.mjs). npm run db:pull
# brings them back locally when a seed or ingest needs to rewrite them.
# backend/db.json
# backend/settings.json
# One db.json per dataset (db.CAPEX.json, ...) - same reason, same place: S3 holds them.
# backend/db.*.json
# The report prototype's dataset, which now lives in the bucket beside the two databases.
# backend/reports_prototype.json

# Local credentials - never commit. Covered by *.local above; named here so a
# stray copy (.backup) cannot slip past it.
#
# These three lines were commented out once and the keys were committed twice as a result, both times
# blocked by GitHub push protection. They are not a preference. A key in a tracked file is scraped off
# GitHub by bots within minutes of a push, and `check-docs` asserts no tracked file matches AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}
# for the same reason. If a credential needs to travel, it goes in the deploy environment, never here.
backend/.env.local
backend/.env.local.backup
